            <ArticleTitle>Biologics in the treatment of chronic pain: a new era of therapy?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>122-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/cpt.20</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Existing analgesics fail to provide adequate pain relief in a significant proportion of patients complaining of chronic pain. Furthermore, their use is limited by tolerability and safety concerns. Thus, there is a huge unmet need for effective and safe innovative painkillers. Considering the major role of nerve growth factor (NGF) in the generation and maintenance of a wide range of pain states, the issue is whether anti-NGF biologics under development might offer such an opportunity.</AbstractText>
